From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: msi: generate transforms and their summary information

An administrator customises a vendor's MSI with a transform (.mst) and
deploys it with `msiexec /i package.msi TRANSFORMS=corp.mst /qn`. Wine
applied transforms but could not make one: MsiDatabaseGenerateTransform
returned ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED and MsiCreateTransformSummaryInfo
failed, so the packaging tools that make them (Orca, InstEd, the transform
editors of deployment suites) could not save their work on this system.

- MsiDatabaseGenerateTransform compares every table of the two databases
  by primary key and writes, in the format msi_table_apply_transform reads,
  its own string pool and a stream per table: changed columns as a masked
  row, new rows whole, removed rows as keys alone; new tables as _Tables and
  _Columns rows; dropped tables as a deleted _Tables row; binary fields as
  streams named after the row's keys. With no file name it only says
  whether the databases differ (ERROR_NO_DATA: they do not). Columns added
  to an existing table are not written yet (a FIXME).
- MsiCreateTransformSummaryInfo writes the transform's summary information:
  title, the reference and new databases' platform;language, the product
  codes and versions and upgrade code check_transform_applicable parses,
  the schema, and the validation and error flags.

Gate: test/msitransform-gate.sh (a package built by the probe, customised,
the transform made, applied, and installed with msiexec TRANSFORMS=; all 5
checks fail without this patch).
